{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792253661,"nonce":"hR/ax4VoeEs543HIivpOprXNoA4=","title":"Python: num_of_box moves earlier operands' hoisted statements after their readers","message":"`num_of_box` takes all of `self.hoisted` to put the hold of the box and the tag guard after what lowering the box hoisted, and returns the result as a block expression. But `self.hoisted` also holds what earlier operands of the same expression hoisted, such as the guarded field read of a call's receiver. Those operands are already built as reads of their temporaries, so in `w.graph.node(i)` with `i` converted from a box, the receiver reads its temporary before the block assigns it. Inside a loop that is the previous iteration's value, and on the first iteration it is undefined (\"type mismatch: expected pointer, got Undef\" in the interpreter).\n\nThe statements must stay hoisted, in order, and the converted value be a plain expression over the held temporaries.\n\nIt fired only while an Object could convert to a Num at a call argument (the refused OTHER escape, 38b017a); hexiom2's `constraint_pass` and the `degree` part of `crates/zyntax_python/conformance/functions/numbers_and_objects.py` reproduce it there.","files":null}]}